A||||16||87 Steve GT||Raced a Honda.. ||||6||
Z||000000||87 Steve GT||01-26-2000||01:46 AM||||Well today as I got off work., which is across the street from the high school.. a bright purple honda civic pulled out reving his motor at me because he's seen me before(87 burgandy GT) I also have a sticker of a lil' boy pissing on a Honda symbol..  lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> so anyway's i caught him just as we reached a long (3/4) mile straight a way. as  passed him I waved .....well I kept going  and about 45 minutes later I came back through there going back to the office and...  on the side of the road sat a smoking.. pruple Honda civic... well of course i stopped to help... he was pretty pissed off as you could imagine... well after i calmed him down... He ended up asking me for a ride to his mother's house... after the ride back in a 1987 gt he was in love with my Fiero..ALL HE DID WAS LOOK the interior and ask ?'s and listen to the hummmm of the motor, he even asked me to turn the radio off so he could hear the motor... he said that he was going to look for one himself... Steve..Tyler,Tx||||reg||6
Z||000001||Standard||01-26-2000||03:42 AM||||That's awesome, man!  one rice-boy converted.. now we just have to find a way to get the rest of the masses into a fiero...||||reg||14
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-26-2000||02:10 PM||||Another soul SAVED from the DAM-NA-TION of the IM-PORT clutches. A young man turned to see the LIGHT of Horsepower and the DEVINE PROMISE...of our beloved torque. Say amen! I said SAY AMEN! RAISE your hands to PONTIAC and its ALMIGHTY mid-engine SAVIOR! A race of 2 cars turns into the saving of FACE for this wayward and lost soul. Say AMEN to another who has joined the GLORIOUS RANKS of the deciples of the P-Body. FIERO HALLELUJAH!!!<P>(I can't breath, Im laughing at myself too  much....)||||reg||6
Z||000003||Patrick||01-26-2000||02:22 PM||||<BR>Why the celebration? The more people who are "converted", the shorter the supply of Fieros. This will only drive the price up. Of course, this isn't all bad for the forum members who already own a half dozen or so, but for the rest of us it's no advantage.<P>I'm saying this partly tongue in cheek, but there is some truth to what I state.||||reg||4
Z||000004||Cooter||01-26-2000||03:19 PM||||I am also a convert. My Civic used to have the header, loud exhaust etc. But after a while, I figured out something. IT IS ONLY A CIVIC!!!! It is not a hot rod. It is very quick, gets great gas mileage but it aint no high performance sports car. But then again, wasn't the Fiero a commuter car?????||||reg||1
Z||000005||87 Steve GT||01-26-2000||05:51 PM||||Well....  Sorry Patrick... I wasn't trying to celebrate at all ... Sorry I thought that FORUM mean't ALL STORY'S .... MY fault for starting something...........||||reg||13
Z||000006||DRH||01-26-2000||06:44 PM||||Steve,<P>I enjoyed your story. Honda tries to race Fiero... blows his car in the process... winds up getting a ride from the car he was racing... starts checking out the Fiero... Gotta love the irony in that!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think Patrick's comment was directed more at the replies to your story. You gotta admit he does bring up a good point... There are a limited (and decreasing) number of Fieros out there... If too many people are "converted", eventually most of us would no longer be able to afford one. Kinda makes you go hmmmm...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||01-26-2000||09:11 PM||||The other side of the blade is that if more people start looking for the Fiero, the mythical promise of the Fiero being a "collector's car" would be fulfiled and that all of those people who are sitting with their Fieros on blocks under covers waiting to sell them for 20 grand would finally be rewarded for their wasting a good car that was meant to be driven.<P>Each new Fiero owner must go through the "Oh God, a Fiero..." and hear all of the stories. This is where the wheat is seperated from the chaff. I doubt there will be an upswing in demand for Fieros as long as uninformed, uneducated (in Fieros) and uninterested people keep spouting the repeated stories that they hear about our Fieros. It makes me sad that this is the way it is wheather or not it is partly humorous. Okay Im done now, sorry.||||reg||2
Z||000008||RICK||01-26-2000||09:23 PM||||WHDFIRO - you had me laughing in the middle of my class, my students are trying to figure out what I'm laughing about.  Your post reminded me of a movie with Dean Martin in it where he was an evangelist, I can't remember the name of the movie.||||reg||10
